// === QUESTION TEXT ===
<p>A fitness center surveyed 40 members of a new exercise program. For each member the staff recorded the number of weeks in the program, `x`, and that member's resting heart rate in beats per minute, `y`. The number of weeks ranged from 0 to 24. The least-squares regression line for predicting resting heart rate from weeks in the program is</p>
<p style="text-align:center">`hat(y) = $interceptY - $slopeMag x`</p>
<p><b>a.</b> Use the line to predict the resting heart rate of a member who has been in the program for `$weeksGiven` weeks.</p>
<p>$answerbox[0] beats per minute</p>
<p><b>b.</b> Which is the best interpretation of the slope of this line?</p>
<p>$answerbox[1]</p>
<p><b>c.</b> Which is the best interpretation of the y-intercept of this line?</p>
<p>$answerbox[2]</p>
<p><b>d.</b> Someone uses this line to predict the resting heart rate of a member who has been in the program for 260 weeks, which is 5 years. Which statement best explains why this prediction may be unreliable?</p>
<p>$answerbox[3]</p>

// === ANSWER ===
$solutionguide = '<p><b>Step 1 - Read the line.</b> The regression line is `hat(y) = ' . $interceptY . ' - ' . $slopeMag . 'x`, where `x` is the number of weeks in the program and `hat(y)` is the predicted resting heart rate in beats per minute.</p><p><b>Step 2 - Substitute the given number of weeks.</b> At ' . $weeksGiven . ' weeks the predicted resting heart rate is `hat(y) = ' . $interceptY . ' - ' . $slopeMag . ' xx ' . $weeksGiven . ' = ' . $predictedHR . '` beats per minute.</p><p><b>Step 3 - Read the slope and the intercept.</b> The slope is -' . $slopeMag . ', so each additional week in the program goes with a predicted resting heart rate that is ' . $slopeMag . ' beats per minute lower. The y-intercept is ' . $interceptY . ', the predicted resting heart rate for a member at 0 weeks in the program, that is, one who has just joined.</p><p><b>Step 4 - Check the range of the data.</b> The members in the sample had been in the program between 0 and 24 weeks. Predicting at 260 weeks is extrapolation, far outside the observed data. Substituting gives `' . $interceptY . ' - ' . $slopeMag . ' xx 260 = ' . $extrapValue . '`, a negative resting heart rate, which is impossible, so the line clearly breaks down outside the observed range.</p><p><b>Answer:</b> a. ' . $predictedHR . ' beats per minute. b. Each additional week of the program lowers the predicted resting heart rate by ' . $slopeMag . ' beats per minute. c. A member at 0 weeks has a predicted resting heart rate of ' . $interceptY . ' beats per minute. d. 260 weeks is far outside the 0 to 24 weeks of data, so the prediction is extrapolation and may be unreliable.</p>';

