<p>A researcher proposes the candidate line `hat(y) = $eq` for predicting a response from a predictor. Let `x` be the $xdesc and let `y` be the $ydesc, measured in $yunit. This line was not necessarily found by least squares. It is only a candidate.</p>
<p>One observation in the data set has `x = $xv` $xunit and an actual value of `y = $yv` $yunit.</p>
