// === NAME - DESCRIPTION: Function Comprehensive - Projectile Height: evaluate a quadratic model, find its real-world domain as an interval, compute the average rate of change, and interpret it ===
// === SET QUESTION TYPE TO: multipart ===

// === COMMON CONTROL ===
$anstypes = "number,interval,number,choices";

$shift = rand(1,2);
$tEnd = rand(4,6);
$bCoef = 16*($tEnd - $shift);
$cCoef = 16*$shift*$tEnd;

$tEval = rand(1,$tEnd - 1);
$sqTerm = 16*$tEval*$tEval;
$linTerm = $bCoef*$tEval;
$hEval = -$sqTerm + $linTerm + $cCoef;

$tLo = rand(0,1);
$tHi = rand(2,$tEnd);
if ($tLo + $tHi == $tEnd - $shift) {
  $tHi = $tEnd;
}
$hLo = -16*$tLo*$tLo + $bCoef*$tLo + $cCoef;
$hHi = -16*$tHi*$tHi + $bCoef*$tHi + $cCoef;
$aroc = $bCoef - 16*($tLo + $tHi);

$answer[0] = $hEval;
$answer[1] = "[0,$tEnd]";
$answer[2] = $aroc;

$questions[3] = array(
  "On average, the ball is rising between $tLo and $tHi seconds.",
  "On average, the ball is falling between $tLo and $tHi seconds.",
  "The height of the ball at $tHi seconds.",
  "The total distance the ball travels between $tLo and $tHi seconds.",
  "The average height of the ball between $tLo and $tHi seconds."
);
if ($aroc > 0) {
  $answer[3] = 0;
  $trend = "rising";
  $signWord = "positive";
} else {
  $answer[3] = 1;
  $trend = "falling";
  $signWord = "negative";
}

// === QUESTION TEXT ===
<p>A ball is thrown upward from a platform. Its height in feet, `t` seconds after it is released, is modeled by</p>
<p style="text-align:center">`h(t) = -16t^2 + $bCoef t + $cCoef`</p>
<p>The model applies from the moment of release until the ball hits the ground.</p>

<p><b>Part a.</b> Evaluate `h($tEval)`. Give your answer in feet.</p>
<p>$answerbox[0]</p>

<p><b>Part b.</b> Find the domain of this model in the context of the problem. Write your answer in interval notation.</p>
<p>$answerbox[1]</p>

<p><b>Part c.</b> Compute the average rate of change of `h` on the interval from `t = $tLo` to `t = $tHi` seconds. Give your answer in feet per second.</p>
<p>$answerbox[2]</p>

<p><b>Part d.</b> Which statement best describes your answer to Part c?</p>
<p>$answerbox[3]</p>

// === ANSWER ===
$solutionguide = '<p>Step 1 - Evaluate. Substitute `t = ' . $tEval . '` into the model: `h(' . $tEval . ') = -16(' . $tEval . ')^2 + ' . $bCoef . '(' . $tEval . ') + ' . $cCoef . ' = -' . $sqTerm . ' + ' . $linTerm . ' + ' . $cCoef . ' = ' . $hEval . '`. The ball is ' . $hEval . ' feet high at ' . $tEval . ' seconds.</p>';
$solutionguide .= '<p>Step 2 - Domain. The ball is released at `t = 0`, and the model stops applying when the ball lands, which is when `h(t) = 0`. Factor: `-16t^2 + ' . $bCoef . 't + ' . $cCoef . ' = -16(t + ' . $shift . ')(t - ' . $tEnd . ') = 0`, so `t = -' . $shift . '` or `t = ' . $tEnd . '`. A negative time is before the release, so the ball lands at `t = ' . $tEnd . '` seconds. The domain is `[0, ' . $tEnd . ']`.</p>';
$solutionguide .= '<p>Step 3 - Average rate of change. Find the heights at the two endpoints: `h(' . $tLo . ') = ' . $hLo . '` and `h(' . $tHi . ') = ' . $hHi . '`. Then `(h(' . $tHi . ') - h(' . $tLo . '))/(' . $tHi . ' - ' . $tLo . ') = (' . $hHi . ' - ' . $hLo . ')/(' . $tHi . ' - ' . $tLo . ') = ' . $aroc . '` feet per second.</p>';
$solutionguide .= '<p>Step 4 - Interpret. The average rate of change is the net change in height divided by the elapsed time. Its sign is ' . $signWord . ', so on average the ball is ' . $trend . ' over this interval. It is not a height, a distance traveled, or an average height.</p>';
$solutionguide .= '<p>Answer: a. ' . $hEval . ' feet. b. `[0, ' . $tEnd . ']`. c. ' . $aroc . ' feet per second. d. On average, the ball is ' . $trend . ' between ' . $tLo . ' and ' . $tHi . ' seconds.</p>';

