$solutionguide = "<p>Step 1 &mdash; Find the slope. Use `m = (y_2 - y_1)/(x_2 - x_1)` with the two points: `m = (($y2) - ($y1))/(($x2) - ($x1)) = ($dy)/($dx) = $mtxt`.</p><p>Step 2 &mdash; Find the y-intercept. Substitute the slope and the point `($x1, $y1)` into `y = mx + b`: `$y1 = ($mtxt)($x1) + b`. This gives `$y1 = $mx1 + b`, so `b = $y1 - ($mx1) = $b`.</p><p>Step 3 &mdash; Write the equation using `m = $mtxt` and `b = $b`.</p><p>Answer: `$eqtxt`</p>";

